Plinius: no Automatic Suspend on the Power page.

plinius-suspend puts the phone to sleep whenever the display is off. The switches "On Battery
Power" and "When Plugged In" set gsd-power's sleep-inactive-*-type, whose suspend goes through
logind instead: a seat pause without a check of the display, and a suspend with the display on
hangs the display driver (docs/STANDBY.md). The device package sets both keys to 'nothing'; the
rows, their delays and the notice about higher power consumption are no longer shown.

diff --git a/panels/power/cc-power-panel.c b/panels/power/cc-power-panel.c
index d27b721..8931a44 100644
--- a/panels/power/cc-power-panel.c
+++ b/panels/power/cc-power-panel.c
@@ -865,6 +865,12 @@ setup_power_saving (CcPowerPanel *self)
 static void
 setup_automatic_suspend (CcPowerPanel *self)
 {
+    /* Plinius: no automatic suspend here. plinius-suspend puts the phone to sleep as soon as the
+     * display is off; gsd-power's suspend after inactivity goes through logind (seat pause, no
+     * look at the display, a suspend with the display on hangs the display driver). The groups
+     * stay hidden (visible: false in the .blp) and their switches unbound. */
+    return;
+
     /* Automatic suspend rows */
     if (self->can_suspend == ACTION_AUTOMATIC && g_strcmp0 (self->chassis_type, "vm") != 0) {
         gtk_widget_set_visible (GTK_WIDGET (self->suspend_on_ac_group), TRUE);
